Title: 200 AMSTERDAM: THE VERTICAL CITY
Credit: Written for the Screen by
Author: Danny Bouldiez
Episode: PART 01: THE GHOST IN THE WALL (CHAPTER 0)

====

INT. COLUMBIA UNIVERSITY - EARTH SCIENCES DEPARTMENT - NIGHT

Rain lashes against the tall arched windows. Cardboard boxes litter the floor of a once-grand professor's office.

ARIS THORNE tapes up the final box. His hands are trembling.

On the wall, a framed certificate: "CHAIR OF TECTONIC GEODETICS - DR. ARIS THORNE". He takes it down, hesitates, and drops it face-down into the trash bin.

                         ARIS (V.O.)
          First came the whisper network in the academic journals. 
          Funded by real estate PACs. Labeling me an 'alarmist crank'. 
          Then the university trustees—three of whom sat on Sterling 
          Development's investment board—stripped my tenured chair.

Aris takes a swig of cheap bourbon directly from the bottle. He glares at his reflection in the dark windowpane.

                         ARIS
          (bitter self-mockery)
          Why are you talking to me like that, Aris? Just go home. 
          Go back to your empty apartment, your empty bottle, your 
          empty miserable life. Nobody cares what the ground is doing. 
          Nobody cares who gets buried as long as the money keeps moving!

He SMASHES the bottle against the radiator. Glass SHATTERS.

                         ARIS (CONT'D)
          (screaming at the empty room)
          WHO THE FUCK AM I SUPPOSED TO BE BEFORE I DIE?!

INT. STERLING PENTHOUSE - 200 AMSTERDAM - CONTINUOUS

70 stories above the rain-slicked city. Marble floors, modern art, floor-to-ceiling glass overlooking Central Park.

JULIAN STERLING (20s, intense, protective) stands between his mother, ELEANOR (50s, frail, tear-stained), and his father, KLAUS STERLING (60s, immaculately tailored, cold as dry ice).

                         KLAUS
          She gets fifty thousand and the lease in Astoria. 
          That is my final offer. Sign the release, Julian, or 
          I cut both of you out of the trust by morning.

Julian steps directly into his father's face.

                         JULIAN
          Look at her, Dad. She gave thirty years of her life 
          to your empire. You have no heart left in you—you've 
          been completely poisoned by the illusion that money is 
          everything.

Julian turns to his mother, his voice softening with fierce tenderness.

                         JULIAN (CONT'D)
          Mom, look at me. You don't need him to be happy. In his 
          eyes, you're just a line item on a balance sheet. But to 
          me, Mother, you are an angel. I'm moving us out tonight. 
          We're going to find a place where we can actually be free.

Julian takes Eleanor's arm and guides her toward the private elevator.

Klaus stands alone in the vast, empty penthouse. High above the city, the wind HOWLS against the glass curtain wall.

Beneath the floor, a single high-tensile steel cable SHIVERS with tension.

FADE TO BLACK.
